  "assembly_and_firmware_notes": [
    "Approved simplified architecture: main devices receive individual external power connections. No Pi, LILYGO, LCD or Chameleon main power travels through this carrier. Use one power source per device; never parallel USB 5 V outputs.",
    "JP2 peripheral supply: 1 +5V_EXT, 2 GND, 3 3V3_AUX, 4 GND. A regulated USB 5 V source feeds CardKB and the VIN of an external preassembled Pololu D24V10F3 #2830. Its regulated 3.3 V output feeds JP2.3. Do not swap either voltage or connect a bare battery cell.",
    "ESP3V3 remains separate from 3V3_AUX. Grounds are common. Both LILYGO VSYS contacts and all 40 Pi header contacts remain NC. The Pi powers its retained HAT through its USB host connection; do not independently backfeed HAT power.",
    "JP3 is an eight-pin harness to the preassembled Adafruit #757 I2C level shifter: 1 GND, 2 ESP3V3/LV, 3 +5V_EXT/HV, 4 SDA_LV/A1, 5 KB_SDA/B1, 6 SCL_LV/A2, 7 KB_SCL/B2, 8 GND. A/B are matched channels, not carrier component reference A1. Unused module channels remain unconnected. This is not the module physical footprint.",
